 (121°C for 20 minutes and 115°C for 50        minutes) and the type of medium (brine and palm oil). The fresh tuna used for canning was caught        from Aceh water. The quality parameters evaluated for fresh tuna were histamine levels, total plate        count (TPC), and pH. Meanwhile, the parameters tested on the quality of the canned tuna were TPC,        pH value, heavy metals lead (Pb) and mercury (Hg) contamination, and levels of consumer        acceptance through organoleptic tests (hedonic). The results indicated that the TPC values for all        canned tuna were <1x101 cfu/g, the metal contaminations were <0.0001 mg/kg for Pb, and in the range        of 0.29-0.58 mg/kg for Hg. The hedonic tests proved that although all the panelists accepted these two        types of canned tuna, they prefer the taste of canned tuna in a salt solution and the color of canned tuna        in palm oil. This research suggests that the sterilization process for canned tuna using a 24L pressure        canner should be carried out at 121°C for 20 min.        KEYWORDS: canned tuna, sterilization, microbial activity, heavy metal contamination, histamine    PENDAHULUAN                                                    km 2 di Zona Ekonomi Ekslusif (ZEE). Hal ini                                                                menjadikan Indonesia sebagai salah satu negara    Indonesia memiliki wilayah perairan laut yang luas          penghasil ikan yang besar (Ghufran & Kordi, 2010). dengan garis pantai sekitar 81.000 km dan mendapat             Salah satu wilayah penghasil ikan terbesar di hak pengelolaan serta pemanfaatan ikan ± 2,7 juta              Indonesia adalah Provinsi Aceh. Potensi hasil laut  Copyright © 2021, JPBKP, Nomor Akreditasi : 30/E/KPT/2018 DOI : http://dx.doi.org/10.15578/jpbkp.v16i1.705                                                                                                                     73 JPB Kelautan dan Perikanan Vol. 16 No. 1 Tahun 2021: 73-8